---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const title = "Government Employees Moving to the Private Sector or Business in India";
const seoTitle = "Government Employees Moving to the Private Sector or Business in India";
const description = "Government employees moving to the private sector or business in India: rules, benefits, risks, skills, a plan and honest limits.";
const seoDescription = "Check service rules and benefits before moving, and test the new work first.";
const canonical = "https://futurecareerschool.com/blog/career-change/government-employees-moving-to-private-sector-or-business-india/";
const publishedDateISO = "2026-10-30";
const publishedDateLabel = "30 October 2026";
const authorName = "Shivanshi Sehgal";
const authorUrl = "https://futurecareerschool.com/about/shivanshi-sehgal/";
const authorRole = "Career researcher and writer";

const faqItems = [
  [
    "Can I do outside work while in government service?",
    "Rules vary. Check your service rules and seek written permission."
  ],
  [
    "What happens to my pension?",
    "It depends on service rules and years of service. Read the official rules."
  ],
  [
    "Which private roles suit me?",
    "Roles using your domain such as operations, compliance and policy. Read notices."
  ],
  [
    "Is starting a business risky?",
    "Yes. Test with a pilot and keep a savings buffer."
  ],
  [
    "How do I avoid fraud?",
    "Never pay for guaranteed jobs or franchises."
  ],
  [
    "How do I avoid fraud?",
    "Never pay for guaranteed placement."
  ],
  [
    "Will AI change this?",
    "It helps learning and planning. Judgement remains yours."
  ]
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: item.a },
  })),
};
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  seoTitle={seoTitle}
  seoDescription={seoDescription}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="career-change"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  jsonLdExtras={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Government employees thinking of moving to the private sector or business must first check service rules on resignation, pension, benefits and permission for outside work, and since these differ by department and state, the careful approach is to read the official rules, map transferable skills, test the new work part time where allowed and then decide.</strong> The decisions that unlock high income opportunities include choosing a branch early and building a high-income skill portfolio of finished work, because AI can handle routine tasks but cannot take responsibility for your results.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Short answer:</strong> Check service rules and benefits before moving, and test the new work first.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> This page quotes no statistics or pay figures and was not built from fetched sources. Ten live notices and two conversations, as set out below, are the best way to get current local evidence.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth:</strong> Clear proof and finished work support an earlier path to financial freedom.</li>
